<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Puhar</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kaveripattinam, Poompuhar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Puhar, also called Kaveripattinam, was the main port of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a> kings at the mouth of the Kaveri River in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Sangam poems such as the Pattinappalai and the epic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silappatikaram">Silappatikaram</a> describe it as a busy harbour where foreign merchants traded. Tradition says the sea later engulfed much of the city, and the modern village of Poompuhar stands on the site.</p></div>
